_meanings:
.²1 Favour, kindness, condescension, propitiousness; {#kuru dfzwiprasAdam#}
 ‘be pleased to show yourself’; {#ityA prasAdAdasyAstvaM paricaryAparo#}
 {#Bava#} <ls>R. 1. 91</ls>, <ls n="R.">2. 22</ls>; {#Druvamatra na varDayet prasAdam#} <ls>Bu. Ch. 5. 65</ls>.
.²2 Good temper, graciousness of disposition.
.²3 Calmness, tranquillity, composure, serenity, sedateness, absence of
 excitement; {#AtmavaSyErviDeyAtmA prasAdamaDigacCati#} <ls>Bg. 2. 64</ls>.
.²4 Clearness, limpidness, brightness, transparency, purity (as of water,
 mind <ab>&c.</ab>); {#gaNgA roDaHpatanakaluzA gfhRatIva prasAdam#} <ls>V. 1. 9</ls>; <ls>Ś. 7. 32</ls>;
 {#prAptabudDiprasAdAH#} <ls>Śi. 11. 6</ls>; <ls>R. 17. 1</ls>; <ls>Ki. 9. 25</ls>.
.²5 Perspicuity, clearness of style, one of the three Guṇas according
 to Mammaṭa, who thus defines it:-- {#SuzkenDanAgnivat svacCajalavat sahasEva#}
 {#yaH . vyApnotyanyat prasAdo'sO sarvatra vihitasTitiH#} <ls>K. P. 8</ls>; {#yAvadarTakapadatvarUpamarTavEmalyaM#}
 {#prasAdaH#} or {#SrutamAtrA vAkyArTaM karatalabadaramiva nivedayantI GawanA#}
 {#prasAdasya#} <ls>R. G.</ls>; see <ls>Kāv. 1. 44</ls>; {#cittaM vyApnoti yaH kzipraM SuzkenDanamivAnalaH .#}
 {#sa prasAdaH samastezu rasezu racanAsu ca#} <ls>S. D. 611</ls>; {#prasAdaramyamojasvi#}
 {#garIyo lAGavAnvitam#} <ls>Ki. 11. 38</ls>.
.²6 Food offered to idols <ab>&c.</ab>, or the remnants of such food.
.²7 A free gift, gratuity.
.²8 Any propitiatory offering.
.²9 Wellbeing, welfare.
.²10 An essence of the food <ab>etc.</ab> (at the completion of the stages of digestion);
 {#rasAd raktaM prasAdajaM, tato raktAnmAMsaM prasAdajaM, mAMsAnmedaH prasAdaja#}
 {#ityAdi yAvat SukAd garBaH prasAdajaH iti#} <ls>Āyurvedaśāstra.</ls>
